<lesson id="les-l8-03-satellite-village" title="The satellite village" level="8" minutes="12" goal="DesaTerpencil joins by satellite and answers between 400 and 600 milliseconds"/>
<step n="1" text="DesaTerpencil has no road for fibre and no line of sight for radio. A satellite terminal already points at the sky, but its cable to the hub was never plugged in. Ping LayananKabupaten from WargaTerpencil and read the failure."/>
<step n="2" text="Cable TerminalLangit FastEthernet0 to HubKabupaten GigabitEthernet0/2. The village joins by satellite." check="c1"/>
<step n="3" text="Ping again and read the time. The signal climbs 36000 kilometres and comes back down: around half a second is normal, and nothing you cable will change that." check="c2"/>
<step n="4" text="Compare DesaMakmur over its radios: well under 20 milliseconds. Pages and messages are fine over satellite; a phone call or a game suffers. Choose what runs where accordingly." check="c3"/>
<check id="c1" kind="ping" from="pc1" to="server0" url="" expect="ok" label="DesaTerpencil reaches LayananKabupaten"/>
<check id="c2" kind="latency" from="pc1" to="server0" url="" expect="600" label="DesaTerpencil answers in under 600 milliseconds"/>
<check id="c3" kind="latency" from="pc0" to="server0" url="" expect="20" label="DesaMakmur, over the radios, answers in under 20 milliseconds"/>
